# E0400: the `idkey` bound admits only the unsigned scalars whose bits ARE an
# index. A reference has none (its low bits are alignment padding), a signed
# integer's are not a count, and a float's are not an integer at all.
main: function is {
    a: (IdMapV String value: u64)
    b: (IdMapV i64 value: u64)
    c: (IdSet f64)
    print "\{a.length} \{b.length} \{c.length}"
}
